+      "id": "container-layout",
+      "title": "Docker application image / docker",
+      "content": "# Docker application image / docker\n\n## Docker application image\n\nThe application image installs Ariadne and its locked runtime dependencies, including the CLI and stdio MCP server. It runs as UID 1000, stores state under `/data`, and reads source under `/workspace`. It includes cloud and local configurations with container paths; the local configuration already contains the serving manifest's artifact pins.\n\nOn 2026-10-11 the image was built and tested on **linux/amd64**. A subsequent [local distribution test](../tests/fixtures/container/2026-10-11/distribution/README.md) pushed it to an isolated registry, pulled it by digest into an empty Docker daemon, and verified the installed package, both Compose configurations and state persistence across container recreation. The CLI/MCP model fixtures run with external networking disabled. External publication is separate from this verification; build the image from this checkout:\n\n```sh\ndocker build -t ariadne:local-model-support .\ndocker run --rm --network none ariadne:local-model-support --help\n```\n\nThe image uses a non-editable installation and pinned Python/uv base images. Host credentials, operator databases, tests and model weights are excluded from the runtime image. Language-specific SCIP indexers/build toolchains are not included; workflows requiring them need a separately provisioned image and writable indexing locations.\n",
